(text_box "1. Function: C51 and C53-C57 put 1 uF on six ASIC rails where they leave for the ASIC stacks (C51, C53, C55, C57 at the J3/J4 ports; C54 beside U5; C56 beside U7). Each returns to the ground the ASIC boards decouple that rail to: C54 (DVDD) to GND, which is the ASIC boards' DGND; the other five to AGND.\n\n2. Source / changes: Claude design (7 Nov review, V20), no manufacturer reference circuit. Changed in V34: C54 moved from AGND to GND, because ASIC boards V6 decouple DVDD to DGND (C7, C14, C61, C62) and every other rail to AGND (read from both V6 board files, 12 Nov 2026); review items LDOA-11 and LDOA-16. V28 (Howard, 9 Nov 2026): C52 (VDD_ADC), C58 (VDD10) and C59 (VSS10) removed; those rails keep their regulators' output capacitors. All are 1 uF 10 V 0402, Samsung CL05A105KP5NNNC, JLC C14445 (JLC stock read 12 Nov 2026, 19:37 CST). Unverified: the capacitor values on the ASIC boards (not yet given by the designer), and the regulators' stability with this extra capacitance at the end of the trace (LT3042/LT3094 are stable with larger output capacitance per their data sheets)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 322 418 0) (size 95 45.9) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "abadae04-f42d-5cbf-9037-d2f02336ec39"))
