(text "ASIC PORTS - TWO ASIC BOARD PAIRS (J3 TOP, J4 BOTTOM, SAME SPOT)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 230 37 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "62acbc93-f394-58d9-82a5-5e3e36725159"))
(text_box "1. Function: Two ASIC board pairs sandwich this board. J3 (plug, top face) feeds the pair above: the bottom ASIC board (ASIC5/ASIC6) and, through its T_ pass-through lines, the top ASIC board (ASIC7/ASIC8). J4 (receptacle, bottom face, same XY) feeds the pair below the same way (ASIC1/ASIC2, then ASIC3/ASIC4). Each port also carries the nine ASIC rails, AC_IN, 2 AGND and 4 DGND contacts (pins 46, 48 and, from V36, 3, 5).\n\n2. Source / changes: ASIC boards V6, bottom and top (12 Nov 2026; built on the designer's updated pair): J3 and J4 carry the same name on each pin number of both boards (pin map V6 check: 0 differences on 80 pins x 4 connectors). Pin assignment: pin map V6 (12 Nov 2026; 2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/09_Pin_Map_V6/PIN_MAP_V6.csv and ASIC_PORT_PINS_V6.csv; frozen 13 Nov 2026). Changed from schematic V30: the designer's final 80-pin order is the old order with the west T_ bus moved by four pins, so pins 2/4/6/8 now carry T_READ(2), T_D<8>(2), T_D<7>(2), T_D<6>(2) and pins 10-22 the lines that sat four pins earlier; pins 24/26/28/30/32/58 carry top-chip lines that had no contact; pins 16/18 and 66/68 are the top chips' own SPI data, pin 70 their SPI latch and pin 72 their SPI clock (meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer A2: not shared with the bottom chips). Pins 3 and 5 (DISC_OUT) are not needed (answer A3). CLKH stays one line per port (BOARD1_CLK, BOARD3_CLK). Unverified: the designer's own check of his board pair; data bit order and READ/SYNC timing (firmware only). V36 (Howard, 16 Nov 2026; pin map V7, 2026-11-16_FPGA_Work/04_; review R2S-05): pins 3 and 5 of J3/J4 are now GND. V43 (Howard, 19 Nov 2026; pin map V8 (2026-11-19_FPGA_Work/10_Pin_Map_V8_One_Latch_Per_ASIC_Board/PIN_MAP_V8.csv)): pin 61 (SPI_LATCH of the bottom board) is no longer one shared net: J3.61 = BOARD3_SPI_LATCH (ASIC5/ASIC6, from J1.36) and J4.61 = BOARD1_SPI_LATCH (ASIC1/ASIC2, from J2.48). The through via that joined the two pads is replaced by a laser via in J4 pad 61; J3 pad 61 is entered on layer 1. Designed by Claude." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 225 530 0) (size 170 50) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "952975f0-ce18-5eb2-8bda-8e3fe145b1f7"))
