(text "U8 LT3042 0.75 V, return AGND" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 600 396.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "eabdd4e6-3956-5710-8664-a98a86029014"))
(text_box "1. Function: Seven regulators make the ASIC rails from VIN_3V3; each rail is shared by all eight ASICs through the two ASIC ports. LT3042 (U2 VDD_FE, U6 REF_VDD, U8 REF_VCM 0.75 V): Vout = 100 uA x RSET. TPS7A2015 (U3 VDD_ADC, U4 VDD_DRIVER, U5 DVDD, U7 VDD_CGEN): fixed 1.50 V. All start from EN_ASIC_RAILS (TPS7A20 EN high above 0.9 V max, LT3042 EN/UV above about 1.24 V). R802 (47k to AGND) is the minimum load of U8.\n\n2. Source / changes: LT3042 cells inherited from Gerald LDO Board A (Reference/LDO Board A/PCB.kicad_sch): IN, EN/UV and PGFB at the input, ILIM to ground, OUT=OUTS, CIN/COUT 10 uF 10 V 0603, CSET 1 uF, PG open, RSET 15k/7.5k; ADI LT3042 data sheet, Typical Application p.1 and Pin Functions, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3042.pdf. Claude changes: EN/UV to EN_ASIC_RAILS; one regulator per rail for eight ASICs. V24 (Howard, 8 Nov 2026, \"find smaller parts\"): U3/U4/U5/U7 changed from LT3042 3x3 DFN cells to TI TPS7A2015PDQNR 1x1 mm X2SON (TI SBVS338H Rev H, Jul 2024: Pin Functions p.4 DQN 1 OUT/2 GND/3 EN/4 IN/5 pad; Recommended Operating Conditions p.5 CIN 1 uF, COUT 1-200 uF with >= 0.47 uF effective; Electrical Characteristics p.7 VEN(HI) 0.9 V max; https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps7a20.pdf); their RSET/CSET (R301-R701, C303-C703) are removed and CIN/COUT are 1 uF 10 V 0402. Trade-off: 7 uVrms against 0.8 uVrms (LT3042), accepted by Gerald 9 Nov 2026 (\"I think its okay to do that\"). V34 (12 Nov 2026): every regulator now returns to the ground its rail is decoupled to on the ASIC boards: U3 (VDD_ADC) with C301/C302 moved from GND to AGND, and U5 (DVDD) with C501/C502 moved from AGND to GND; the other five were already on AGND. Basis: ASIC boards V6 decouple DVDD to DGND (C7, C14, C61, C62) and every other rail to AGND (read from both V6 board files, 12 Nov 2026); meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer B3 (two grounds, joined at one point on this board); review items LDOA-11 and LDOA-16. REF_VCM stays LT3042 because 0.75 V is below the TPS7A20 0.8 V minimum. Loads of REF_VDD/REF_VCM unknown. V36 (Howard, 16 Nov 2026, review item SYS-61 / fix P1, \"as long as it does not change the size\"): 0.6 mm test pads TP11, TP12, TP14-TP17 on VDD_FE, VDD_ADC, DVDD, REF_VDD, VDD_CGEN, REF_VCM. V37 (layout V18): TP13 (VDD_DRIVER), TP18 (VDD10), TP19 (VSS10) dropped, no room in the outline; probe C402, C902, C1002 instead. V41 (19 Nov 2026, pre-fabrication review V2 and Zitong Xu): R802 47k 1 % 0402 (Uniroyal 0402WGF4702TCE, JLC C25792, 4,838,934 orderable, read 19 Nov 2026 07:48 CST) added from ASIC_REF_VCM to AGND: 0.75 V / 47k = 16 uA, above the 10 uA minimum load the LT3042 needs for stability when VOUT is below 1 V (same data sheet, Electrical Characteristics, Minimum Load Required and Note 13, p.5). Designed by Claude; not in the inherited or data-sheet circuit. Unverified: the REF_VCM current of the ASIC itself and the output noise with this load." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 422 402 0) (size 300 40.5) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3a175775-280f-57b3-93ca-71a1e64f3781"))
