(text "U9 +8.06 V on ASIC_VDD10 (LT3042)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 470 254.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "84754b70-ee07-5fa3-a052-7af626efea21"))
(text "U10 -8.06 V on ASIC_VSS10 (LT3094)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 560 254.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d876b625-a10a-5667-a3ce-fd12a3645970"))
(text_box "1. Function: U9 (LT3042) makes ASIC_VDD10 = +8.06 V from STIM_PRE_POS; U10 (LT3094) makes ASIC_VSS10 = -8.06 V from STIM_PRE_NEG (the net names are kept from the +/-10 V revisions). Both are referenced to AGND and start with EN_ASIC_RAILS. Each serves the stimulators of all eight ASICs (about 8 mA at Gerald's 2 mA per board maximum).\n\n2. Source / changes: U9 inherits Gerald LDO Board A U8 (LT3042, RSET 90k, input from an external INPUT_VDD10); U10 replaces LDO A U9 with a true negative LDO. ADI LT3042 data sheet, p.1 Features and Typical Application, p.3 Electrical Characteristics, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3042.pdf ; ADI LT3094 data sheet Rev 0 (2018), p.1 and p.4, Pin Functions p.15, https://www.analog.com/media/en/technical-documentation/data-sheets/lt3094.pdf . Both set the output as 100 uA x RSET (SET pin current 100 uA, +/-1 % initial; output range 0 to 15 V and 0 to -19.5 V). Changed from the data sheet p.1 circuits: RSET 80.6k (was 33.2k), CSET 1 uF (was 4.7 uF); PGFB to IN, ILIM to ground, PG and VIOC open; EN/UV from EN_ASIC_RAILS. V34 (Howard, 12 Nov 2026: stimulation rails +/-8 V, the level the ASIC designer runs from a battery; meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer B4): R901/R1001 changed from 100k to 80.6k 1 % 0402, Uniroyal 0402WGF8062TCE, JLC C25921 (124,346 orderable, JLC stock read 12 Nov 2026, 19:37 CST); 100 uA x 80.6k = 8.06 V. An exact 80.0k 0402 is not in JLC stock. With 1 % parts and 1 % SET current the rails lie between about 7.9 and 8.2 V. Checks for 8 V: U1 is the fixed LT3582-12 and stays at +/-12 V (factory set, data sheet 3582512fb p.1), so each LDO has about 3.9 V of headroom against a dropout of 350 mV (LT3042) and 235 mV (LT3094) and inputs far inside 20 V; the extra loss is about 4 V x 8 mA = 32 mW per regulator. The 0.8 uVrms (10 Hz-100 kHz) noise figure is specified for 1.3 V <= VOUT <= 15 V and -19.5 V <= VOUT <= -1.5 V with CSET 4.7 uF, so it does not depend on the 8 V setting; here CSET stays 1 uF. Output capacitors unchanged (C902 22 uF 25 V 1206; C1002 22 uF 1206 plus C1004 10 uF 25 V 0805; LT3042 needs >= 4.7 uF, LT3094 >= 10 uF). Unverified: noise measured at the ASIC pins; effective capacitance from the Samsung DC-bias curves at 8 V; no clamp or bleed on the rails at power-down (review items LDOA-08, -09, -28: not changed in V34)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 627 218 0) (size 110 80.1) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5449a649-df8d-5622-b245-73632add8c27"))
