(wire (pts (xy 539.75 43.18) (xy 534.67 43.18)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid "958cd2d8-73d3-5518-813d-fcbaf7a3898f"))
(text_box "1. Function: C1/C2 hold VIN_3V3 for the converter and regulators; it arrives on J2.68-70, the three Frontend supply contacts. R1/C3 delay EN_ASIC_RAILS by about 20 ms after VIN_3V3, so all nine ASIC rails start after the frontend 1.5 V bank supply. NT1 is the only AGND-GND bond for all four ASIC boards (the ASIC boards must not add their own).\n\n2. Source / changes: Claude design, no manufacturer reference circuit. Delay: tau = R1 x C3 = 47 ms; LT3094 EN/UV turns on at 1.26 V, so t = 47 ms x ln(3.3/2.04) = 23 ms; LT3042 threshold assumed similar (to confirm). Nine EN/UV pin currents x 10k must stay well below 1.26 V. The frontend VCCO_1V5 start time is not measured. NT1 follows the LDO V13 NT100 single-bond idea; the ASIC boards carry AGND (42/44) and DGND (46/48) separately on J3/J4 and no part on them joins the two (read from the V6 board files) (checked in its PCB file). V34: meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer B3, confirms two grounds joined at one point on this board, far from the chip; NT1 stays the only bond. C901/C1001 return to AGND and the LT3582 capacitors to GND, so part of the converter ripple still crosses NT1 (review items LDOA-10, LDOA-12: not changed in the schematic; layout V13 found no legal site for plane vias at NT1). Unverified: ripple between AGND and GND at the ports, and whether VIN_3V3 sags at the J2 contacts (0.9 A for three)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 410 60 0) (size 135 43.05) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d1e4dfbd-4511-525f-881f-84bc45780e77"))
(text "ASIC CONTROL SAFE IDLE" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 585 24 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "48137be3-6185-5b68-b3c0-47edf4bc962f"))
