(text_box "1. Function: Hold every FPGA-to-ASIC control line at its safe level while the FPGA is unconfigured: STIM_EN/START/CHB/CLK, FE_RESET, IMP_TEST and SPI_LATCH low; CHIP_RESET high (to ASIC_DVDD), so the ASICs stay in reset until the FPGA releases them. About 150 uA per line when driven to the other level.\n\n2. Source / changes: Claude design from Gerald's firmware (Archive/.../07_FPGA_512_Reference/repository/fpga): top_custom.v section 3b drives CHIP_RESET high for 2^20 cycles (~65 ms) at boot then low (active high); line 264 holds FE_RESET low (\"amplifier reset released, normal operation\"); STIM_* held low; custom_board.lpf line 100 leaves IMP_TEST an input with PULLMODE=DOWN; spi_programmer.v keeps SCLK idle low and pulses LATCH high. Needed because the Frontend ties PUDC_B high (R25 470R), disabling FPGA pull-ups during configuration (AMD UG470, PUDC_B). V23 adds R16-R23 to V22's R2-R5. V28 (Howard, 9 Nov 2026) had dropped the four clock pulls R20-R23; V34 brings them back with four more for the top chips, drawn in the block ASIC CLOCK AND TOP-CHIP SPI SAFE IDLE. READ/SYNC are ASIC outputs and get no pull. Unverified: ASIC input leakage and thresholds; reset polarity is from firmware, not an ASIC data sheet." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 702 28 0) (size 82 54.45) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "45aff1a0-51f4-564c-b836-385adb6c113f"))
(text "AC_IN DEFAULT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 699.48 103.22 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "12760e75-76c0-5c6b-9e45-2384e4a4484f"))
