(text_box "1. Function: R6 holds the analog AC_IN input of all eight ASICs at AGND; TP7 lets a bench source inject a test signal (0-1.5 V nominal) through the shared node.\n\n2. Source / changes: Claude design. The Frontend has no AC_IN source and no connector contact for it (V43), so AC_IN is handled here. V21: in version B these parts sit on the router, so AC_IN needs no J5 contact. Nominal 0-1.5 V from ASIC_REFERENCE.md section 4 (relayed designer answer). Gerald, 9 Nov 2026: \"0V is the right state. No need to care about input impedance or anything else.\"" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 699.48 123.22 0) (size 90 28.8) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "811b9aca-3659-586a-8af9-7b3f0dfd344d"))
