(text_box "1. Function: R20-R28 hold the FPGA-to-ASIC clock and latch inputs that had no pull at a low level while the FPGA is unconfigured or a line is undriven: the fast clock CLKH of both ports (BOARD1_CLK, BOARD3_CLK), the bottom chips' SPI clocks (BOARD1_SPI_CLK, BOARD3_SPI_CLK) the top chips' own SPI clocks and latches (ASIC3_4_TOP_SPI_CLK/LATCH, ASIC7_8_TOP_SPI_CLK/LATCH) and, from V43, the own latch of port J3's bottom board (BOARD3_SPI_LATCH, R28). About 150 uA per line while it is driven high.\n\n2. Source / changes: Claude design, no manufacturer reference circuit; same part as R2-R5/R16-R19: 10k 1 % 0402, Uniroyal 0402WGF1002TCE, JLC Basic C25744 (16.2 million orderable, JLC stock read 12 Nov 2026, 19:37 CST). Reason: the ASIC designer said the chip pads have no internal pull resistors (meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md), answer C2), so this board must set every level; review items LDOA-49 and SYS-28. R20-R23 return the four clock pulls that V28 removed (Howard, 9 Nov 2026); R24-R27 are new for the top chips' own SPI clock and latch of pin map V6 (port pins 72 and 70). Idle-low follows Gerald's firmware (spi_programmer.v keeps SCLK low and pulses LATCH high). Not pulled: the 16 SPI data inputs (STIM_CHIPn_SPI_DL/DR, ASICn_SPI_DL/DR); they are only taken in on an SPI clock edge and a latch pulse, and both are now held low. Unverified: ASIC input leakage and thresholds; the designer gave no preferred idle level (answers C1, C3, C4: \"should not matter much\"). All eight are placed and routed in layout V13. R23 sits on the top side beside R4, tapped at contact J2.13; the other seven are on the bottom side. V43 / layout V24 (Howard, 19 Nov 2026, \"cool this is good\"; pin map V8 (2026-11-19_FPGA_Work/10_Pin_Map_V8_One_Latch_Per_ASIC_Board/PIN_MAP_V8.csv)): R28, same part (C25744, 30.1 million orderable, read 19 Nov 2026, 11:07 CST), pulls the new line BOARD3_SPI_LATCH (J1.36 / FPGA ball V14 to J3.61) low; the old shared line keeps R18 as BOARD1_SPI_LATCH (J2.48 to J4.61). Reason: the designer sends one SPI clock and latch per board (meeting with the ASIC designer, 12 Nov 2026 (2026-11-12_FPGA_Work/07_Meeting_With_ASIC_Designer_V1/MEETING_NOTES_V1.md)). Designed by Claude. R28: bottom side, north-west corner. Unverified: the 32 mm lane (layer 2 west edge, layer 1 north edge) is not measured." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 565 454 0) (size 130 68) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9edb9274-829c-542f-9c8a-7eb97b984eb7"))
(text "5 V PROVISION (UNUSED)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 420 526 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) (bold yes)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fa51a849-bb94-5da4-a68f-3b050879cb5d"))
