no part, no paste) on the bottom face, reachable with the ASIC stacks and the Frontend mated (bottom face y >= 117.1 mm). TP20-TP22: ASIC4 SPI_DR, SPI_DL and DATA1 at port J4; TP24: ASIC3/ASIC4 SPI clock; TP25: STIM_START; TP27: BOARD1_SPI_LATCH (the latch of port J4; probe BOARD3_SPI_LATCH on R28); TP28: FE_RESET. TP23, TP26, TP29: GND returns for the scope ground spring; TP30, TP31: AGND returns for the analog rails (C53/C402, C902, C1004, TP8). Positions and the nearest probe points of the other lines: PROBE_MAP.csv in the layout V20 record.\n\n2. Source / changes: Designed by Claude for bring-up probing, per Howard 18 Nov 2026 (professor: every board needs scope test pads, Open Ephys ONIX headstage test board as the example); no manufacturer reference circuit. New in V39: TP20-TP31 on existing nets (no new nets, no part moved); 0.1 mm stubs up to 0.95 mm long, GND stub 0.2 mm. Not placed (no room without moving parts): BOARD1/3_CLK (CLKH), CHIP_RESET, STIM_EN/CLK/CHB, the other SPI lines (use the R2-R5, R16-R27 pull-down pads) and VDD_DRIVER, VDD10, VSS10 (use C402, C902, C1002). Unverified: probe loading and ground-spring length (TP20-TP22 sit 3.2-4.9 mm from TP23)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 733 453 0) (size 53 70) (margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0712d466-2ebb-4579-b60d-0652da867643"))

 

